# Esper Origins cast with flashback, copied by Lutri, the Spellchaser flashed in over it. The copy surveils 2 and gains 2
# life, but a copy is not cast (CR 707.10), so "if this spell was cast from a graveyard" is false for it: it exiles nothing
# and puts nothing onto the battlefield, and ceases to exist as it leaves the stack (CR 707.10a). The original, cast from
# the graveyard, then does all of it: one Summon: Esper Maduin with one finality counter. Three resolutions of "you gain 2
# life" in all (the cast from the hand on turn 1, the copy and the original): 26 life.

